1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,337
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:09,009
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,561
I want to say goodbye to all of you.

7
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,312
Take care of yourself, Ibyang, okay?

8
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:24,107
[Karla] Study well. Don't be like me.

9
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,776
[Ibyang] <i>Thank you for everything, Tatoy.</i>

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:27,861
[sobs]

11
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:30,572
<i>I love you, Tatoy!</i>

12
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:32,198
[Atoy] <i>What are you still doing here?</i>

13
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,199
<i>Huh?</i>

14
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:36,453
<i>Your mother is waiting.</i>
<i>You need to go to her.</i>

15
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:37,370
‪PREVIOUSLY

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:41,916
[Ibyang sobs] Tatoy…
I just want to hug you again.

17
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,042
[sobs]

18
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:46,171
[Atoy] <i>You'll always be stitched</i>
<i>right here in my heart.</i>

19
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,505
[Red] <i>As long as we have Ibyang,</i>

20
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:49,632
<i>Atoy can't do anything against us.</i>

21
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,342
Eventually, the child
has to be disposed of.

22
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,677
What do you mean, disposed of?

23
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:54,512
Get rid of her, so there's no trace.

24
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:55,764
[Charmi] <i>Have you thought about it?</i>

25
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:57,682
<i>Where could Ibyang's real mother be?</i>

26
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:00,060
Now you ask,
when you already have the money.

27
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,227
Forget it.

28
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,395
Is Atoy there?

29
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:06,524
[Emerson] <i>We are just drowning</i>
<i>his sadness. He invited us.</i>

30
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,986
Fried dumpling,
with vinegar and sweet sauce.

31
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,905
That's what you should buy.

32
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:14,657
[Olga] <i>You opened</i>
<i>the imported corned beef?!</i>

33
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:18,161
Oh, no! Why did you do that?!

34
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:21,539
Just like that,
they're suddenly taken away.

35
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,124
I can handle being alone.

36
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,668
[Gonzales, in English] I was ordered
by Colonel Mercado to meet you

37
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,003
and deliver his directives.

38
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:32,383
[Samir, in English] I want you to find out
everything about this man.

39
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:36,346
[in English] Then, we will find him.

40
00:01:37,847 --> 00:01:41,184
[in English] I'm sure
he is looking for the decoder.

41
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:42,936
[music swells]

42
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:44,062
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

43
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:46,147
[Olga] Oh, and now you're crying?!

44
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,774
It's your fault!

45
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:53,655
[sobbing]

46
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,581
I'm sorry.

47
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,959
[sobbing]

48
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:09,838
I'm sorry.

49
00:02:09,921 --> 00:02:11,256
[sobs]

50
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:16,970
Tatoy taught me that the house
should always be tidy.

51
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,222
I'm not your father!

52
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:21,808
We're different, okay?!

53
00:02:24,018 --> 00:02:25,103
[Olga] Go on!

54
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:26,646
[utensil clatters]

55
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:28,940
[sighs] Let's not waste
this meal you cooked.

56
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:33,403
You're so young yet you already know
how to do so many things.

57
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:38,158
Do you know how to do laundry?

58
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,618
Yes.

59
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:44,581
Sis Ame and I used to do laundry together.

60
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:51,504
[Ibyang] Mama. May I ask something?

61
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:54,132
No.

62
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:58,094
Then, just tell me a story.

63
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:02,682
Where is my father?

64
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,726
Why aren't you with him?

65
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,854
- [scoffs]
- Do I have a grandmother?

66
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,315
What's your favorite color?

67
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,608
[sneaky music playing]

68
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:13,735
You're good at segueing questions, huh.

69
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:19,157
Anyway, you don't have a father!

70
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,074
Okay?

71
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:27,081
Do you want Tatoy instead?

72
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:29,792
He's single now.

73
00:03:30,793 --> 00:03:31,836
Hmm?

74
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:33,963
With that handsome face?

75
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:37,175
[Ibyang] He's just grumpy.

76
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:40,929
And he does a lot of strange things.

77
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:44,474
What else does a tailor do?

78
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:48,811
[music fades]

79
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:51,898
[Mercado] <i>Padua,</i>
<i>you have a follow-up mission.</i>

80
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:56,277
<i>I sent Lieutenant Gonzales</i>
<i>to hand you a device.</i>

81
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:01,199
This is the device I extracted
from the Zahran embassy, sir.

82
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:02,492
Why is this here again?

83
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:04,911
[Mercado] <i>I'll send you</i>
<i>the mission details.</i>

84
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:09,123
<i>But this laptop is for safekeeping</i>

85
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:12,961
<i>until you find Ms. Lily Santiago,</i>

86
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:15,672
<i>who is in charge of this device.</i>

87
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:17,173
[in English] All right. Copy, sir.

88
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,800
<i>Thank you, Padua.</i>

89
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:21,427
[in English] <i>I will keep you posted</i>
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

90
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,720
[in English] Copy, sir.

91
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,848
[suave theme music playing]

92
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:27,767
[motorcycle revving]

93
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,686
[sewing machine whirring]

94
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,566
[sewing machine clacking]

95
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:38,945
[gunshots]

96
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,118
[music swells]

97
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,420
Ibyang used to do that.

98
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:59,632
She helped me carry the groceries.

99
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:05,555
But actually, she was just waiting
for rice cakes as a treat.

100
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:06,931
[chuckles]

101
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:11,477
And also, she was really kind.
That's why I miss her.

102
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:14,939
Even if she was a bit naughty,
she was still kind.

103
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:18,318
I hope Olga is taking good care of her.

104
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:19,777
Oh, you're here.

105
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:25,241
Well, miss, even though
we're not related by blood,

106
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:27,827
we grew to love that girl so much.

107
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:30,413
So, her real mother
must love her even more.

108
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,081
[sighs]

109
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:33,166
Oh!

110
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:34,834
How's Atoy?

111
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:38,755
Good thing you don't have a hangover
from last night's drinking.

112
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:42,675
- Ah. It ended early.
- Huh?

113
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:47,430
Because his boss sent someone.

114
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,849
He has a new assignment.

115
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:51,267
And he accepted it.

116
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:54,103
Maybe to distract himself
from Ibyang leaving.

117
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,147
Ah. Oh.

118
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,942
Are you Miss Cita?

119
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:02,779
Ah…

120
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:04,322
Yes, that's me. Who are you--

121
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:06,991
- Please, help me!
- [stammering]

122
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:09,327
Please, help us!

123
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:10,828
[Emerson] Wait, wait.

124
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,916
You were referred to us
by your former client.

125
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:17,877
The one who looked
for his child who eloped.

126
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,631
He said you have contact
with the Master Cutter.

127
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,758
- You?! You're the Master Cutter?!
- [quirky sting]

128
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:25,510
- Master Cutter, help us!
- Oh!

129
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:26,511
No, I'm not.

130
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:28,137
No, no. I'm not.

131
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,223
- Oh.
- [sobs]

132
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:32,141
Oh, oh, come inside.

133
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,184
[sobs]

134
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,352
Come in.

135
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:37,355
- [sobbing]
- [muttering]

136
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:46,864
My child…

137
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:51,828
[in English] I have a surprise for you!

138
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,539
[in English] Are you ready?

139
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:56,874
[Audrey] Open it.

140
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,210
[in English] What's this?

141
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:00,419
[in English] Open it!

142
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,674
[in English] It's your passport!

143
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:06,968
Really, Mommy?!

144
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,929
So, when are we leaving?

145
00:07:10,012 --> 00:07:11,681
Once we get your visa.

146
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,182
[in English] I already
applied for it online.

147
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,976
From there, it will be fast.

148
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:20,106
- I'll finally see snow in real life!
- [Audrey chuckles]

149
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:23,484
Child.

150
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:27,405
Do you want to say goodbye to your daddy?

151
00:07:28,364 --> 00:07:29,532
[in English] No.

152
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:30,533
Come on, child.

153
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,826
At least call him.

154
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:34,036
[in English] You…
You might not see each other…

155
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:36,706
again.

156
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:38,583
It's okay.

157
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:39,876
He's bad anyway.

158
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:42,420
He hurt Grandpa, right?

159
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,089
My child.

160
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:48,217
[in English] That was an accident.

161
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,972
Because he wanted to hurt Uncle Red.

162
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:54,348
He's still bad.

163
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:57,977
I never felt his love for me.

164
00:07:58,769 --> 00:08:03,232
[inhales] So, it's okay
if we don't say goodbye to him.

165
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:05,651
[pensive music playing]

166
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,487
He loves you, Janine.

167
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:12,783
Believe me.

168
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,578
[somber music playing]

169
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,413
[in English] Okay.

170
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:21,375
[pensive music playing]

171
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,172
Go ahead, eat.

172
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,061
[music fades]

173
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,272
Drink first.

174
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:44,482
[woman sniffles]

175
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:54,200
We came here
because we're so desperate, Miss Cita.

176
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:56,661
[sobbing]

177
00:08:56,744 --> 00:09:03,209
We're the administrators
of the Build for Kids organization.

178
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:07,547
We have a project to build
a school in Zambales.

179
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:12,969
We already gathered money from sponsors.

180
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,221
[wails]

181
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:20,101
But we lost the money we saved.

182
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:22,562
It was stolen.

183
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:23,771
[wails]

184
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,147
[somber music playing]

185
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:30,778
You should go to the police
so those responsible can be charged.

186
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:31,737
[sobs]

187
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,614
We already did.

188
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:39,495
But the investigator said
our lead was a dead end.

189
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:41,038
Ah.

190
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:43,749
We just want to recover the money.

191
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,919
We don't want this to become a news item

192
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:51,299
because we don't want to lose
the trust of our sponsors.

193
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,883
[clears throat]

194
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:57,305
So, ah, how much money
are we talking about here?

195
00:09:58,347 --> 00:10:00,057
[in English] Five million! [wails]

196
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:01,767
- [in English] Five million pesos?!
- [in English] Five million?

197
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:06,147
So please, help us.

198
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,566
For the sake of the children

199
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:10,443
who'll lose their chance to study

200
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:12,612
if the school doesn't get built.

201
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:13,863
[sobs]

202
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:15,698
Oh my God.

203
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:18,242
That's such a huge amount--

204
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:20,036
[suspicious music playing]

205
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:24,874
But the Master Cutter
isn't here right now.

206
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:27,084
He already has another assignment.

207
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:30,212
It's over! We have no hope
of recovering it.

208
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,214
[sobs]

209
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:33,633
[clears throat] Uh…

210
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:35,384
Uh, well…

211
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:36,844
[stutters]

212
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,054
Uh, maybe, ah--

213
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,055
[titters]

214
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,473
Maybe… Maybe--

215
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:41,557
[stutters]

216
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:46,854
Ah… Calm down.
We'll try to contact another tracker.

217
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:50,149
Uh, maybe he can help you.

218
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:51,984
Please stop crying. Stop crying.

219
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:53,819
Huh?

220
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,196
Who?

221
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:56,280
‪[quirky sting]

222
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:57,865
The…

223
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:59,158
The… The son.

224
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:01,911
The son… son of the thread.

225
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:03,412
That! That's the one…

226
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:07,166
He was also trained by the Master Cutter.

227
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:11,629
[stammers] Maybe he can help you
recover your money.

228
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:14,548
Really? Oh, thank you.

229
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:16,967
[in English] Thank you.

230
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:18,427
[in English] Thank you. Thank you!

231
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:20,679
[in English] Thank you! Thank you!
[giggles]

232
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:21,847
[titters]

233
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,474
Calm down, calm down.

234
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:25,184
Yes… Yes, okay.

235
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:29,939
[sneaky music playing]

236
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:30,856
‪[quirky sting]

237
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:33,275
Son of the thread?

238
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:41,534
Oh, all right. We'll update you, okay?

239
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:42,660
- Thank you very much.
- Okay.

240
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:43,577
Take care.

241
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:45,121
- [in English] Thank you.
- Thank you.

242
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:51,419
Emerson.

243
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:56,715
Who is this "son of the thread"
you're talking about?

244
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:00,845
You gave those two hope
that there's another tracker here.

245
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:04,056
Miss, I didn't give them false hope.

246
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,392
They will actually be helped by…

247
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,310
- the son of the thread.
- Ah!

248
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:10,187
So, who is it?!

249
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:11,981
Me.

250
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:13,774
- Eh, you! you…
- [chuckles]

251
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:16,193
- You're always full of nonsense!
- [Emerson] Miss.

252
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:18,779
You gave those two women
false hope, poor thing--

253
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:21,031
Miss, I'm not kidding around.

254
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:22,992
I know what to do!

255
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:24,952
I've joined Atoy's missions many times.

256
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,245
I know this already!

257
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:27,997
I've joined about…

258
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:31,125
- [Cita] What?
- About… Twice. Two times!

259
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,376
Miss, I know what to do.

260
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,086
- That's easy for me!
- [claps hands together]

261
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,546
Really, huh?

262
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:36,547
Fine.

263
00:12:37,339 --> 00:12:44,013
What do you do when searching
for a missing person or thing?

264
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,516
Aside from praying to--

265
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,685
- [Cita] Mmm? Mmm?
- to Saint Anthony of Padua.

266
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:51,729
- [Emerson] What…
- What?

267
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:53,105
Eh…

268
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:56,609
[sneaky music playing]

269
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,319
Oh, no. Oh, no.

270
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:00,070
- You nailed my irritation!
- Wait-- I know--

271
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:02,531
- You really nailed my irritation!
- [Emerson] I know, miss, I know!

272
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:03,741
Miss, eh.

273
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:04,867
- [Cita] What?
- I'll call Atoy.

274
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,160
I'll ask him for help.

275
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,244
That's better, otherwise,

276
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:09,413
- you will get it from me.
- Atoy.

277
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:10,956
Atoy.

278
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,750
[music fades]

279
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:16,462
[camera shutter snapping]

280
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:19,590
[suspicious music playing]

281
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:23,969
[phone ringing]

282
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:26,347
- [line ringing]
- Hmm, you think you're so clever.

283
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:27,973
Miss, it's ringing. Be quiet.

284
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,475
[line ringing]

285
00:13:29,558 --> 00:13:31,143
[phone rings]

286
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,438
- Hello?
- Ah! He… Hello?

287
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:35,898
Atoy.

288
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:37,816
'Toy, please help me.

289
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:39,735
Please.

290
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:42,488
What happened to you?

291
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,949
You sound like your life is in danger.

292
00:13:45,032 --> 00:13:49,119
It is in danger, in Miss Cita's hands.

293
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,454
Serves you right.

294
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,206
- Huh?
- Nothing.

295
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,916
[Atoy] <i>What's going on? What do you need?</i>

296
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:57,294
No. Well, 'Toy, it's because, um…

297
00:13:57,378 --> 00:14:02,299
Someone came here
asking for help, looking for you.

298
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:03,217
‪Uh…

299
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:07,972
But you weren't here.
They said they were robbed.

300
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:10,933
So, I volunteered.

301
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,059
What?!

302
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,018
[Emerson] <i>Yes!</i>

303
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:15,020
Because, of course, I felt bad for them.

304
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:17,314
They asked for help, and…

305
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,483
[Emerson] <i>It's for a good cause.</i>

306
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:25,030
Because the stolen money
was meant to build a school for children.

307
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:26,574
So, ‘Toy, what? Will you help…

308
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,909
Help me, ‘Toy, okay?

309
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,077
Will you help me?

310
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:33,163
[sneaky music playing]

311
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:36,292
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

312
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:38,002
There, huh. You said it, huh. Okay.

313
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,461
[in English] Step by step, ‘Toy, okay?

314
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,505
This will be a long talk.

315
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:43,757
Son of a thread.

316
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,635
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

317
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,305
[Atoy] <i>Here's what you do.</i>

318
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:56,186
There. Take a look.

319
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,647
- Take a look.
- Right.

320
00:14:59,773 --> 00:15:02,526
[Atoy] <i>Observe how the theft happened</i>,

321
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:04,528
<i>how they entered the place.</i>

322
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:06,614
<i>Look closely at the thief too.</i>

323
00:15:06,697 --> 00:15:08,908
<i>Usually, their faces are covered, so…</i>

324
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:12,119
<i>look for other clues on their body.</i>

325
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:32,181
Unbelievable.

326
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:39,730
We worked so hard to secure sponsorships,
to save money for the children.

327
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:44,735
Why are there people
who don't know how to fight fair?

328
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:55,829
Well, you know their day will come.

329
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:07,758
Here.

330
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:09,051
[in English] Sixty.

331
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,344
That's too expensive.

332
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:11,512
Make it 50!

333
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:13,514
Vegetables are pricey.

334
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:15,015
[in English] Fifty-five!

335
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,100
[in English] Fifty-six!

336
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:17,768
[in English] Fifty-three!

337
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:19,979
Fine!

338
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:22,856
[sneaky music playing]

339
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,233
Hey, wait!

340
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:26,151
No backing out, miss!

341
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:27,903
You already agreed!

342
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,905
If you back out now,

343
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:32,032
your luck might back out too!

344
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,410
You're a clever kid.

345
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:41,542
Can you teach me how to cook chop suey?

346
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:45,129
Wow! You haggled
and now you want a tutorial.

347
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:46,630
Where's your mother?

348
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:49,091
Why don't you ask her to teach you?

349
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,467
Whose child are you?

350
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:54,179
Mama Olga. The one who lives there.

351
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:56,640
Oh, I know Olga.

352
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:58,100
Are you her child?

353
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:02,563
Yes, we just reunited.

354
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:05,232
We were separated when I was a baby.

355
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,110
But now she found me.

356
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:09,945
Wow, like a soap opera!

357
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:13,407
But Olga never told us
she had a missing child.

358
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,242
Where did you come from, kid?
How old are you?

359
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:17,077
[Charmi] Oh my! Oh!

360
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:20,622
Ibyang, what are you doing here?

361
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:24,293
Sister Faye,
I just bought food for dinner.

362
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:26,879
Oh, Ibyang.

363
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:30,007
Don't talk to gossips,

364
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:32,176
or you'll end up like them.

365
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:34,803
Go home now.
Your mama won't like this. Go home now.

366
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,555
[in English] Go.

367
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:38,557
Hey, Charmi! Why did she call you Faye?

368
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,726
Hey, you!

369
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:43,771
That's my second name, Charmielyn Faye!

370
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:44,897
You're such a gossip.

371
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,148
You ask too many questions!

372
00:17:46,231 --> 00:17:47,608
I forgot what I was buying.

373
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:50,736
Here, here! Give me plantains.
I'll make pot roast today.

374
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:51,987
Okay.

375
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,113
There, let's put it in a plastic bag.

376
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:54,907
Oh, come on. Okay.

377
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:57,785
- Here.
- Hmm.

378
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,496
- Take care of it.
- Yes.

379
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:04,208
Ma'am, who do you think
would be interested in this money?

380
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,627
Who else knows about it?

381
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,212
Our staff.

382
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,714
But they've all been investigated.

383
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:14,760
No one suddenly resigned
or changed lifestyle.

384
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:17,221
We have one suspect.

385
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:21,058
It's hard to accuse anyone without proof.

386
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:24,436
Then make an accusation.
It's just us here anyway.

387
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:27,731
The ex-president of Build for Kids.

388
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:29,983
He was bitter when he was replaced.

389
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:34,905
He swore we'd never have
a successful project without him.

390
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:36,907
[pensive music playing]

391
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,784
Do you have a picture of this person?

392
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,744
Yes we have. Wait.

393
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:43,122
Here he is. There.

394
00:18:43,205 --> 00:18:45,415
Kevin Martinez.

395
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:53,423
Um, good afternoon,
Ma'am Malou, Ma'am Odette.

396
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,550
[Emerson] Uh…

397
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:57,344
Sir, are you investigating the theft?

398
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:02,057
Any updates?

399
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:06,228
Still none.

400
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:08,939
Honestly, the longer this case drags on,

401
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:11,817
the smaller the chance
we'll recover the money.

402
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:15,529
Most likely, it was already spent.

403
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:20,284
- [sobbing]
- [tense music playing]

404
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:28,292
[music fades]

405
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:29,710
Brother Atoy left right away.

406
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,004
We didn't even get to talk.

407
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:34,464
Just wait for him to come back.

408
00:19:35,048 --> 00:19:36,717
But what if he doesn't?

409
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:39,261
His missions are dangerous.

410
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:43,182
I only feel at ease when I'm with him,

411
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:45,809
when I'm driving him.

412
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:48,520
At least then, I know he's safe.

413
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,314
[suspicious music playing]

414
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:51,565
[Atoy] Who's that?

415
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:53,108
Later, brother! Let's go!

416
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:55,819
[gunshots]

417
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:57,613
Hey!

418
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:59,072
[gunshots]

419
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:06,205
But now it seems unlikely
he'll take me along again.

420
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,623
Wait, wait, wait.

421
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:10,584
You said you're Brother Atoy's driver,

422
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:12,502
and his missions are dangerous.

423
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:15,756
Does that mean he's the boss you mentioned
in Endless Nights before?

424
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:16,757
Huh?

425
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:20,427
The one in the shootout,
then jumped out of the car?

426
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:21,762
That was Brother Atoy?

427
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:23,263
I never said that.

428
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,352
Karla, wait.

429
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,146
Don't deny it.

430
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,731
I won't tell anyone.

431
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:34,483
It's me, after all.

432
00:20:35,442 --> 00:20:38,070
That's the problem. It's you.

433
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:40,614
Well, you did slip a bit
to Brother Atoy last time.

434
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,824
It won't happen again.

435
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,576
[in English] Promise?

436
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,328
[light music playing]

437
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:47,579
[in English] Promise.

438
00:20:48,205 --> 00:20:49,206
[in English] Okay.

439
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:52,376
But Brother Atoy's side job is top secret.

440
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:57,089
I didn't want you to know,
because isn't your dad his enemy?

441
00:20:57,798 --> 00:20:59,508
They almost killed each other.

442
00:20:59,591 --> 00:21:01,260
I won't tell Dad.

443
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:04,721
Actually, I prefer what Brother Atoy does.

444
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,890
Exposing Endless Nights.

445
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:09,309
At least he shut it down

446
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:12,020
and stopped the boxing match
of little persons.

447
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:14,815
You know…

448
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,402
you're really different from your dad.

449
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:22,281
Let's promise each other
that whatever conflicts happen

450
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:24,283
between your brother and my dad,

451
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,952
our friendship won't be affected.

452
00:21:27,035 --> 00:21:28,495
We're solid.

453
00:21:28,578 --> 00:21:29,579
[in English] Okay?

454
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,581
[in English] Promise?

455
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:36,169
[chuckles softly]

456
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,179
There.

457
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,683
[in English] Promise.

458
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:54,271
[music fades]

459
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:57,899
[suspicious music playing]

460
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,154
[chuckles softly]

461
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:03,905
Karla, let's stay here first.

462
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:05,073
[Karla] Why?

463
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:09,703
[music fades]

464
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:11,830
What? What?

465
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:14,291
You see I'm concentrating here.

466
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:18,045
You've been replaying that over and over.

467
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,796
So? Did the ending change?

468
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,256
Here!

469
00:22:22,132 --> 00:22:24,343
I can't focus!

470
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:25,886
That sweeping is irritating!

471
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,554
Sweep later.

472
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:31,141
Just admit, you're too ambitious!

473
00:22:31,224 --> 00:22:33,226
You're acting like the Master Cutter.

474
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,395
Atoy's level is here.

475
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:37,606
Yours is way down here!

476
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,816
You can't reach it.

477
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,026
How high?

478
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:43,195
Here, you can't reach it.

479
00:22:43,278 --> 00:22:45,572
It's too high.

480
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:47,991
Oh, you have a problem with being small.

481
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:50,702
But you're only a little taller than me!

482
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:52,204
Here, oh… Come on.

483
00:22:52,287 --> 00:22:53,330
Here, oh.

484
00:22:53,413 --> 00:22:54,498
Oh, try to reach my ear.

485
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:55,457
[chuckles]

486
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,667
Try to reach my ear.

487
00:22:57,751 --> 00:23:00,003
You, do that later.

488
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,630
Just sweep later!

489
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:04,132
There you go again.

490
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,759
Because there's still so much mess!

491
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:07,803
[in English] Special delivery!

492
00:23:07,886 --> 00:23:10,180
Two orders of pares!

493
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:11,848
Huh? Two?

494
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:13,016
Oh, why?

495
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,309
Did you order for me too?

496
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:17,145
No, I'll eat it all myself.

497
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:19,773
Come on. Ouch! What the hell? Ouch!

498
00:23:19,856 --> 00:23:20,774
Stop!

499
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:22,317
[in English] Sorry, sorry.

500
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,069
- Sorry, it was just a joke.
- [in English] You're welcome.

501
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,445
It was just a joke.

502
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:27,405
[sneaky music playing]

503
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:29,324
Put it there, Ame!

504
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:33,495
There, oh!

505
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:36,081
Why do you have CCTV footage here?

506
00:23:36,164 --> 00:23:37,958
[action music playing]

507
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,793
Do you have a mission?

508
00:23:39,876 --> 00:23:41,962
But isn't Atoy gone?

509
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:45,423
I can't solve this without Atoy.

510
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,843
Maybe Ame is right.

511
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:51,930
Maybe I should back out of this mission!

512
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:56,893
Ah, don't! What?! What! what?!

513
00:23:57,936 --> 00:23:59,229
You've been…

514
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,731
Ame, give me that pares!

515
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:05,569
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

516
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:14,786
[music fades]

517
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:18,707
[electronic blipping]

518
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:28,008
We found the suspect
in the five-million robbery.

519
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:29,801
Here's what you do.

520
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,469
You need to go to that shop.

521
00:24:31,553 --> 00:24:33,513
[Atoy] <i>Pretend to be customers</i>
<i>or whatever you want.</i>

522
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:35,056
The important thing is to get inside

523
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:38,476
and gather information
about the money from that person.

524
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,770
[Atoy] <i>Just make sure you're not noticed.</i>

525
00:24:41,396 --> 00:24:45,025
Who's that? Come out…
if you don't want to get hurt.

526
00:24:45,108 --> 00:24:46,902
UP NEXT

527
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:48,403
[in English] You are not a suspect, no.

528
